comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T03:22:00.759Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: a complete 2,597-item all-status strict read and exact-version search found no owner for greptile 3.4.2 or @types/node 26.4.0. Closed pm-7xfndr is the latest compatible refresh lineage; open unclaimed pm-ksr40d and pm-do5b remain the distinct canonical incompatible-major owners. Live pnpm outdated and zero-alert inventories justify this focused compatible patch child."
  "2026-08-29T03:39:40.364Z","harness:codex","Compatibility and performance evidence: package resolution now adopts greptile 3.4.2 and @types/node 26.4.0 while preserving the published @types/node >=22 compatibility range. Full coverage passed. Direct static assurance passed every source/export/member docstring, duplication, package, SDK, contract, defect-evidence, graph, and record assertion; only the final RSS transport ratchet exceeded its fixed margin locally. A same-tree seven-sample A/B on the previous 3.4.1/26.3.0 versions reproduced the same get overage, proving the signal is not caused by these patches. The committed budget remains unchanged and exact-head hosted CI will independently arbitrate the environment-sensitive gate."
  "2026-08-29T03:46:20.444Z","harness:codex","Linked-test harness evidence: pnpm quality:static and the pnpm lint aggregate both intentionally read the real PM corpus for defect governance, so schema-isolated linked execution reported zero governed terminal defects. Both failed runs are retained. The directly executed real-tracker static gate passed every assertion except the independently A/B-reproduced RSS ratchet. Future linked acceptance now contains only coverage, build, ESLint, and duplication commands that are valid in schema isolation."
  "2026-08-29T03:48:08.891Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: pnpm outdated now contains only npm-package-arg 14.0.0 (pm-ksr40d) and TypeScript 7.0.2 (pm-do5b); pnpm audit reports 0 vulnerabilities at every severity; GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning open alert inventories are each 0. Exact coverage passed 586 files and 8,108 tests at 100/100/100/100. Linked build, ESLint, and two-scope duplication gates passed. Packed npx smoke passed all 13 packages; package-first dogfood passed 88 commands; a fresh tarball installed and ran under Bun 1.3.11 via bunx. Hosted exact-head checks remain the environment-independent final transport ratchet."
  "2026-08-29T08:19:29.740Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit exact-head finding: the acceptance criteria require hosted checks and exact-head review, but the item closed while those proofs were still pending. Reopened until the final post-fix head is green and reviewed."
  "2026-08-29T08:44:09.507Z","harness:codex","Local acceptance evidence after the exact-head review fixes: strict static quality passed; full suite passed 586 files and 8,115 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; PM test-all passed 8 executions with 2 duplicate skips and zero failures. Item remains in progress until the new pushed head completes hosted CI and reviewer arbitration."
  "2026-08-29T08:52:18.894Z","harness:codex","Performance-gate evidence: the post-close static run passed every preceding gate but the default three-sample CLI transport floor exceeded the 512 KiB RSS margin by only 130,048 bytes; an isolated three-sample rerun also varied across get/claim. A 20-iteration median rerun then passed all six operations without changing budgets, confirming host/process sampling noise rather than a durable dependency or CLI regression. Hosted CI remains the required arbitration."
  "2026-08-29T10:00:30.389Z","harness:codex","Post-review local evidence: exact coverage passed at 60,152/60,152 statements, 45,379/45,379 branches, 12,511/12,511 functions, and 57,922/57,922 lines. A fresh npm-packed tarball installed in an isolated temporary project; npx and bunx both reported 2026.8.28, and the published SDK import executed successfully under Node and Bun. The temporary project was removed after verification. Hosted exact-head checks and fresh reviews remain the closure boundary."
  "2026-08-29T10:03:35.933Z","harness:codex","Live dependency recurrence: @sentry/cli 3.7.0 appeared after the earlier inventory. Complete all-status PM search found closed historical Sentry refresh pm-4dz7 and the currently claimed same-day compatible refresh pm-vwuidf; no duplicate created. Upstream 3.7.0 requires Node >=18 and contains IPA dSYM upload, snapshot selective-upload, and docs fixes, so it remains compatible with this repository."
  "2026-08-29T10:18:56.305Z","harness:codex","Final local verification evidence before hosted review: exact full-suite coverage passed at 60,152/60,152 statements, 45,379/45,379 branches, 12,511/12,511 functions, and 57,922/57,922 lines (100/100/100/100). The complete repository static-quality chain passed, including build, contract/generated-surface parity, package SDK boundary, graph composition, record integrity, refusal closure, token budgets, and performance floors. Security scan reported no credential-like secrets; pnpm audit reported no vulnerabilities; live GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning inventories were empty. pm-changelog refreshed to registry version 2026.8.29 and verified CHANGELOG.md unchanged for 2,240 closed items. Manual packed-package acceptance in an isolated temporary directory passed npx, bunx, Node SDK import, and Bun SDK import. @sentry/cli 3.7.0 reports successfully and its 113 focused tests pass."
